.TH loadjpg 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
loadjpg \- draw a JPEG on the screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loadjpg
.I file
[\fIx\fR [\fIy\fR [\fImode\fR [\fIximage\fR [\fIyimage\fR [\fIscale\fR]]]]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B loadjpg
decodes a JPEG and draws it with its top left corner at
.IR "x y" ,
0 0 by default.
.I ximage
and
.I yimage
start the picture at an offset within the image.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I scale
1, 2, 4 or 8.  The picture is binned by this factor as it decodes, so a
640x480 photograph fits a 320x240 screen at
.I scale
2 without a separate scaling pass and without the memory a full-size
decode would need.
.TP
.I mode
Read and ignored.  It holds its place in the argument list; it selects
no dithering.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# loadjpg photo.jpg
# loadjpg photo.jpg 20 10
# loadjpg photo.jpg 0 0 0 0 0 2
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loadpng (1),
.BR loadimage (1),
.BR saveimage (1)
